1. Code ported from public Kaggle notebooks (Apache License 2.0)

   The image decoder and the 2.5D window generation of the inference notebook
   (inference/decoded/p26_decode.py, embedded in
   inference/late-l34-tau-l14.ipynb) are a port of two public notebooks by
   dreaddevelopment:

     https://www.kaggle.com/code/dreaddevelopment/knee-mri-twelve-findings-from-a-single-model
     https://www.kaggle.com/code/dreaddevelopment/knee-mri-training-the-twelve-finding-model

   Kaggle releases public notebooks under the Apache License 2.0. Each ported
   function names, in its docstring, the lines of the notebook it was copied
   from. The CoAtNet training recipe of the whole-knee members follows the
   second notebook.


2. Pretrained backbones (Apache License 2.0)

   The members fine-tune two timm / Hugging Face checkpoints:

     coatnet_rmlp_2_rw_384.sw_in12k_ft_in1k
     convnext_small.in12k_ft_in1k_384

   Neither is in this repository. The fine-tuned weights are published as
   Kaggle Datasets (see README.md), each with the backbone's licence text.


3. Training labels of five members (CC BY 4.0)

   The five whole-knee members of the late submissions L14 and L34 were
   retrained on "RSNA Knee MRI LLM Soft Labels for 4407 Studies" by drizlo
   (the 21st place solution), version 1, CC BY 4.0:

     https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/drizlo/rsna-knee-mri-llm-soft-labels

   The labels are not included here.


4. Competition data and label definitions

   The models were trained on the RSNA Knee Abnormality Detection competition
   data, used under the competition rules (section 4, Competition Data) and the
   RSNA MIRA Dataset Research Use Agreement (http://rsna.org/mira-license).
   This repository contains no competition data: no images, reports, labels,
   predictions or study identifiers.

   labels/p8_prompts.py quotes the threshold wording of the competition's
   published label definitions.

   For research and education only. Not for clinical use and not for diagnosis.
